      "title": "How text to 3D works",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Text to 3D with Hyper3D Gen2\n\n1. Describe the object in English (up to 400 characters): what it is, its materials and colors, and that it is complete and fully assembled.\n2. Run. Generation takes a few minutes and is billed per task.\n3. The model opens in the 3D viewer on **Save 3D (Advanced)**: orbit it, then use the viewer's export button to download it in another format. A copy is also saved to your ComfyUI output folder.\n\nmesh_mode **Quad** gives clean, editable topology; **Raw** gives triangles. Open the advanced inputs for exact face counts, HD textures, 4K textures (HighPack) and a T-pose for characters.\n\nNeeds a ModelArk key in Settings > BytePlus. Fixed seed reuses unchanged cached outputs."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": ""
      },
